<title>BELGIUM: EU ruling cuts 0.26 pct from Italian deficit.</title>
<headline>EU ruling cuts 0.26 pct from Italian deficit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eurostat, the EU's statistical office, said on Monday that a review of budget accounting procedures would trim 0.26 percent off the Italian government's 1997 budget deficit.</p>
<p>Specifically, decisions affecting the &quot;capitalised interest on deposits&quot; and the treatment of zero coupon bonds would cut the Italian government's deficit by 0.26 percent of total output.</p>
<p>The statistical body, however, said it was not able to specify the precise amount of money saved from the individual rulings.</p>
<p>A decision on Italy's proposed &quot;euro tax,&quot; meanwhile, is due by the end of February.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 32 2 287 68730</p>
</text>
